        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಇಡ್ಲಿ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಇಡ್ಲಿ — iḍli — \"an idli\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಇಡ್ಲಿ (iḍli) is native Dravidian, one word with Tamil iṭṭali and Malayalam iṭṭali (DEDR 455). DEDR lists iḍḍali, iḍḍalige, a steamed cake of rice flour and black gram. DEDR 455 compares Sanskrit iṇḍarī."
            }
          ]
        },
